  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of labour administration to promote effective social dialogue and dispute prevention and resolution procedures</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Barbados has a long-standing commitment to social dialogue and tripartism through its Social Partnership, which has signed consecutive social contracts since 1990. While the Social Partnership has been an effective governance model, several challenges in its operation and impact exist. To address these challenges, the ILO will facilitate  an assessment of  the Social Partnership with the aim of developing a plan of action to strengthen its effectiveness and inclusiveness. In addition, the ILO will conduct a labour administration needs assessment to improve the Ministry of Labour&apos;s services.

Beneficiaries include workers, employers, and the broader community, with the work being done in collaboration with the Ministry of Labour, the Employment Rights Tribunal, and other national stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
